{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirModeCountFunctor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirModeCountFunctor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirZetaPrefactor","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimirTransportedFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimirTransportedFunctor","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L130-L151","doc":"**Transported consistency witness — NOT a substrate derivation.**\nThis inhabits `PlateModeCountFunctor` with the *textbook* Casimir energy\ndensity hardcoded, `f(A,d) = −A·π²/(720 d³)`. Its only purpose is to show\nthe interface is **consistent** (the two axioms are jointly satisfiable,\nso the class is not vacuous) and that the downstream chain\n(`CasimirEpsilonVacuum`, and via `energyPerArea_deriv` the force law)\nruns end-to-end on a concrete object.\n\nIt is **transport, not derivation**: the `−π²/(720 d³)` scaling is\n*postulated* here, copied from standard physics, **not** produced from\nsubstrate data. Providing it as an instance would let `typeclass`\nresolution silently discharge the conjecture, so it is deliberately a\nplain `def` (not an `instance`). The open conjecture\n(`conj:casimir-epsilon-vacuum`) is precisely that the categorical\nYekutieli lift yields *this* function from the plate-bounded mode count\n— see `docs/workplans/2026-06-12-n-odot-construction-scoping.md` (Stage C).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimir_coefficient_eq_zeta_prefactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimir_coefficient_eq_zeta_prefactor","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L120-L128","doc":"**Bridge to the Stage-B prefactor.** The `d⁻³` coefficient `π²/720`\nof the per-area scaling is exactly the transverse geometric factor\n`π²/6` times `ζ(−3) = 1/120` — i.e. the mode-count's leading coefficient\n*is* the `CasimirZetaPrefactor` value. This ties the Stage-C interface to\nthe machine-checked Stage-B arithmetic (`riemannZeta_neg_three_re`), so\nthe one numerical constant the construction rests on is no longer free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.ofData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.ofData","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L104-L118","doc":"**Stage-C reduction — the two external inputs, made explicit.** A\n`PlateModeCountFunctor` is fully determined by (1) an area-extensive\ncount function and (2) the analytic fact that its per-area part has the\nregularized cubic-tower scaling `−π²/(720 d³)`. Input (2) packages the\ntransported physics — the free-field `n³` mode degeneracy and the\nζ-regularization of the divergent tower (classical Casimir 1948) — which\nis exactly what the open Yekutieli lift must supply. This constructor\nexhibits the reduction: closing Stage C means producing `f` together\nwith these two proofs (no further data). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.force_per_area_of_functor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.force_per_area_of_functor","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L96-L102","doc":"The force per unit area follows from the functor interface alone, by\ncomposing the derived `CasimirEpsilonVacuum` instance with\n`energyPerArea_deriv`: `∂_d (energy/area) = π²/(240 d⁴)` for `d > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.modeCountDiff_extensive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.modeCountDiff_extensive","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L87-L94","doc":"Area-extensivity of the total energy, as a standalone consequence:\nthe total Casimir energy between plates of area `A` is `A` times the\nper-area density. This is the content that makes the *force per unit\narea* a well-defined observable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimirEpsilonVacuum_of_functor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimirEpsilonVacuum_of_functor","kind":"instance","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L76-L85","doc":"**`N_⊙ ⇒ CasimirEpsilonVacuum`.** The plate-mode-count functor's\nper-area archimedean image is exactly the `CasimirEpsilonVacuum` energy\ndensity. Hence constructing `N_⊙` (the open lift) discharges the\ndownstream conjecture class — and, via `energyPerArea_deriv`, the\ntextbook force law `−π²/(240 d⁴)`. This is the precise sense in which\n`N_⊙` is the genuine *upstream* target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.per_area_scaling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.per_area_scaling","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L73-L73","doc":"the per-area count reduces to the disjoint-unknot (bare-count,\nq-free) value selected by `n`-stability: the leading parallel-plate\nscaling `−π²/(720 d³)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.extensive_in_area","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.extensive_in_area","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L69-L69","doc":"extensivity in plate area: the count difference is proportional to\narea, so energy per unit area is well-defined and area-independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.modeCountDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.modeCountDiff","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L66-L66","doc":"archimedean image of `(N⊙^in − N⊙^out)·ε` for plates of area `A`,\ngap `d` (units `ℏc = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.PlateModeCountFunctor","kind":"class","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirModeCountFunctor.lean#L49-L74","doc":"**Stage-C interface for `N_⊙(A, d)`** (§3b-cond class). Carries the\narchimedean image of `(N⊙^in − N⊙^out)·ε` as a function of plate area `A`\nand gap `d` (units `ℏc = 1`), exactly as `CasimirEpsilonVacuum`\nsidesteps the surreal layer by recording the standard-part. The two\naxioms are the content the lift must deliver:\n\n* `extensive_in_area` — the count difference is proportional to the plate\n  area (locality / functoriality of the lift), so the per-area energy is\n  well-defined and area-independent;\n* `per_area_scaling` — the per-area count reduces to the q-free\n  disjoint-unknot value `−π²/(720 d³)` selected by `n`-stability\n  (`CasimirNStability`), with prefactor pinned by `CasimirZetaPrefactor`.\n\nNo instance is provided: the construction is the open Yekutieli lift. ","signatureChunk":0}]}